+The retained prototype adds one episode-fixed `panel_threshold` setting with exact values `1`, canonical/default `2`, and `3`. It reuses the approved fixed-rule generator for inputs, pins generator and canonical Racket hashes, materializes one exact Racket program per setting, and labels both selected and rival behavior through Racket. Demonstrations and queries are independently sized; every sampled input contains panel counts 1, 2, and 3, so the declared finite rivals are refuted by demonstrations rather than by hidden query answers.
